From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 14:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] luma: Super+A and Super+Tab show every desktop as a Grid-style
 card, and the app grid is gone

Owner report: Super+A opened the stock overview's app grid, with the
workspace thumbnails pushed to the top at mismatched heights (the ultra-wide
beside the 1.25x panel), then an icon grid with a page arrow.

Super+A and Super+Tab now open lumaWorkspaceOverview.js: every desktop is a
rounded card on a plain kit surface (#21252b dark, #f2f3f5 light, following
the app colour scheme), live previews of the primary display's wallpaper and
windows, one height for all cards. One or two desktops use Grid's own card
height; the height shrinks only as far as needed to fit three across, and a
longer row scrolls (wheel, two-finger scroll, press-and-drag with fling,
arrow keys, Home/End, 1-9) with the next card peeking in at the edge. The
current desktop is labelled Current and starts selected. Click, Return or
Space switches with the card zooming out to fill the display; Escape, a click
on the surface, Super+A again or a three-finger swipe down zooms back. The
desktop is switched behind the view, and Mutter's slide is suppressed while
it is open. Holding Super, Tab and Shift+Tab step and releasing Super
switches; a tap leaves the view open, as Grid does. Previews reuse Grid's
RoundedPreview, including its fix for textures cached at another display's
scale. Reduced motion makes every transition one frame. Dynamic workspaces
show their trailing empty desktop as New Desktop.

Cards show the primary display only. Luma ships workspaces-only-on-primary,
so the other displays are the same on every desktop, and a composite of an
ultra-wide, a portrait panel and a laptop produced the odd, unequal shapes
the owner reported. The panel and dock stay visible, as with Grid.

Keybindings: org.gnome.shell.keybindings gains toggle-workspace-overview
(<Super>a, <Super>Tab) and toggle-workspace-overview-backward
(<Shift><Super>Tab). toggle-application-view now defaults to nothing, and the
shipped override sets org.gnome.desktop.wm.keybindings switch-applications to
<Alt>Tab only, so Alt+Tab stays Grid and nothing is bound twice. The app grid
is no longer reachable: Overview.showApps() (a rebound Show Apps key, D-Bus
ShowApplications, extensions) opens Luma Search, the app launcher reached by
tapping Super. Dragging windows between desktops is not offered here; the
window menu and Super+Shift+Page Up/Down still move them.

Generated against the Shell .87 tree (0127 applied) for release .88.
---
diff --git a/data/00_org.gnome.shell.gschema.override b/data/00_org.gnome.shell.gschema.override
index ac732e6..7a1f657 100644
--- a/data/00_org.gnome.shell.gschema.override
+++ b/data/00_org.gnome.shell.gschema.override
@@ -4,3 +4,9 @@ edge-tiling=true
 dynamic-workspaces=true
 workspaces-only-on-primary=true
 focus-change-on-pointer-rest=true
+
+# Luma: Super+Tab opens the workspace overview (org.gnome.shell.keybindings
+# toggle-workspace-overview), so the app switcher, Grid, keeps Alt+Tab only.
+[org.gnome.desktop.wm.keybindings]
+switch-applications=['<Alt>Tab']
+switch-applications-backward=['<Shift><Alt>Tab']
